# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BLASTI Mobile App — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file documents ALL environment variables used by the Capacitor mobile app.
# Copy this to .env and fill in your values.
#
# NOTE: The mobile app wraps the web app in a native Android/iOS shell.
# Most configuration comes from the web app's NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── DEVELOPMENT ─────────────────────────────────────
# URL of the Next.js dev server for live reload during development.
# Set this to your computer's LAN IP address.
# Example: "http://192.168.1.100:3000"
# When set, the mobile app loads from this URL instead of bundled static files.
# When empty (production), it loads from the bundled static export.
# CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL="http://192.168.1.100:3000"

# ─── API CONNECTION ──────────────────────────────────
# The URL the mobile app uses to connect to the API.
# This must be a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable so it's embedded in the web build.
# Set this BEFORE building the web app for mobile export.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://blasti.yourdomain.com"

# ─── BUILD ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to "export" to produce a static export for Capacitor.
# This is set automatically by the build:android script.
# NEXT_BUILD_MODE="export"

# ─── ANDROID SDK ─────────────────────────────────────
# Path to your Android SDK installation.
# ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Android/Sdk"
